# Nix / direnv
.direnv/

# Logs of scripts/run-tests.sh. Inside the repository so that a run is easy to
# find, and ignored so that it stays out of the source that every
# nanopynix-tests-* derivation reads with `cd ${../.}`.
.test-runs/

# Reports and diagnostics that a test run writes into the repository root.
# `ci/steps.nix` writes each one and uploads it as a CI artefact, and nothing
# reads any of them back. All five were tracked until now, so every run put
# its output into the working copy and a later commit carried it: one of them
# added about 6000 lines of noise to a commit that changed no test.
coverage.xml
junit.xml
gc-thread-debug.log
test-gdb-output.log
nanopynix-test-store-paths.txt

# The three that the list above did not name. `ci/steps.nix` writes them into
# the same directory, from the TSan legs: `tsan-output-<version>.log` at line
# 257, `tsan-output-broad-<version>.log` at line 325, and one
# `soak-<version>-run<seed>.json` for each seed at line 276. A local run of
# `ciSteps.<version>-tsan` writes them too, so a developer got the same
# result. One commit then carried a 610 KB TSan log and ten soak reports.
# `nix/clean-source.nix` repeats these three rules, and a self-check keeps
# the two files in agreement.
tsan-output-*.log
soak-*.json

# A jj workspace that lives inside the repository. `jj` knows its own
# workspaces and never offers one, so `jj st` stays silent, and only a `git
# add` sees it. One workspace holds a whole second checkout.
.workspaces/
